// stimulus/ — input current and event sources.
//
// Outside core, these reference nothing but neuron/ parameter bundles: a
// stimulus is configured with a cell model (balanced drive, current injection,
// Poisson drive for a given IF or Tripod), so naming that model's parameter
// struct is part of the interface rather than an implementation detail.
//
// The three `stimulus_poisson_layer_*` variants are the same population source
// wired to three different cell models (IF, BallAndStick, Tripod).
//
// empty_stimulus.mbt is the null object -- a stimulus that does nothing, for
// tests and for wiring a model before its real input exists. It carries an
// `nn.EmptyParam`, so nn/ is imported for that one type; that is the only
// reason this manifest reaches above core/ and neuron/.
//
// A pre-split scan called this package dependency-free, which was wrong for the
// reason it has now been wrong three times: the scan only sees references that
// are still inside the root package, and neuron/ had already moved out.
import {
  "riantr/snn_mbt/core",
  "riantr/snn_mbt/neuron",
  "riantr/snn_mbt/nn",
}
